  "failure_mechanism": {
    "headline": "At the primary rung the conditional head is degenerate: it predicts the short-remaining bucket for 92% of survivors on SWE277 (3006 of 3273) and 95% on SWE100 (865 of 910), so it collapses onto the majority classifier it was supposed to beat.",
    "why": "At 1000 ms the surviving population is still dominated by short remaining durations, so every backoff node's values are mostly short and the argmax lands on bucket 0 regardless of the key. There is not yet enough elapsed time for survival to have reshaped the evidence.",
