  "limitations": [
    "Development-exposed; not a confirmation claim. Declared as the final planned read of the two SWE corpora.",
    "Remaining-duration prediction is a much harder and better-balanced task than total-latency bucketing: majority is 39-50% here against 84-88% there. Accuracy figures are not comparable between the two objectives.",
    "The secondary-rung pattern is non-monotone (2000 passes, 4000 fails, 8000 passes) and tracks how peaked the class mix is at each rung, so it should not be read as a clean trend.",
    "A properly powered test of the later rungs needs a criterion frozen in advance and data not yet used; these corpora are spent."
  ]
}
